  "summary": "Decorative elements on Gnaoua ritual instruments featuring symbolic patterns and materials.",
  "description": "Gnaoua instrument ornamentation includes carved and painted designs on guembri (three-stringed bass lute) and metal decorations on krakeb (iron castanets), featuring symbolic patterns and spiritual motifs. The ornamentation reflects Sufi Islamic influences, pre-Islamic African spiritual traditions, and serves both aesthetic and ritual purposes in Gnaoua ceremonies.",
